# {{ .Vars.plans_dir }}/ — what we intend to build

Detailed, and allowed to change. Writing a plan with an agent takes hours rather than
days, so the old tradeoff between planning and speed does not apply the way it used
to. Plan more than feels economical, and expect to revise it.

A plan is the artifact that does the most work in this repository: it gives every
person and every agent the same account of what is being built, why it matters, and
what must be true before the work is accepted.

## Filename grammar

`TYPE-kebab-slug.md`, uppercase type. `PLAN-billing-rewrite.md`, `SPEC-webhooks.md`.

## What a plan contains

The shape is not enforced beyond frontmatter, but a plan that omits these is usually
the one that goes wrong:

- **Outcome** — what is different when this is done, in terms a stakeholder would use.
- **Boundaries** — what this explicitly does not cover.
- **Decisions** — the choices already made, so nobody relitigates them. Link to
  `DEC-*.md` in `../{{ .Vars.docs_dir }}/` for the ones with lasting consequences.
- **Slices** — the next few units of work, each small enough to finish.
- **Acceptance criteria** — per slice, checkable. "Done" is a claim; these are the
  evidence. A criterion nobody can evaluate is not a criterion.

## Frontmatter

```yaml
---
id: plan-billing-rewrite
title: Billing rewrite
status: active               # proposed | active | done | dropped
updated: 2026-08-06
---
```

Links to other record documents are checked: a plan referring to a document that was
never written is drift, and `ilk check` will say so.

```
ilk record new {{ .Vars.plans_dir }} "Billing rewrite"
```
